  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows a strong positive spike (e.g., >82) followed by neutral sentiment; forecasts consistently overshoot the subsequent mean-reversion trend.",
    "Forecasts fail to account for volatility clustering, predicting smooth linear growth while true outcomes show sharp reversals and high-frequency oscillations within 30 days.",
    "When sentiment history contains a single positive spike (1.0) followed by zeros, the model overweights this signal, resulting in forecasts that drift significantly higher than actual realized paths.",
    "Mean reversion is systematically underestimated; models project continued upward momentum even when recent price action indicates exhaustion of gains.",
    "Horizon-specific error: 30-day forecasts are structurally too optimistic by approximately 5-10 EUR compared to true outcomes during periods of high historical volatility."
  ]
}
